From 1111b8402080cea8b0da54dcc268dfcce42d014a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:54:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(import): log a curved STEP face the fit cannot
 measure, mark reduced fidelity

When the curved-face fit (#2600) cannot read a face's mesh (no
parameters, parameters that miss the points, a facet that is not a
triangle, ...), it kept the kernel's facets with no log line and full
fidelity. The fit now names the reason; the import logs the face and
the reason, and reports the face UNMEASURED, so the model is reduced
fidelity and verify refuses.

Fixes #2719

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
